10101010 # instruction | STOSB | AA writes AL to ES:DI and advances DI.
01000001 # instruction | INC CX | 41 increments the bounded input length in 16-bit mode.
11101000 10110010 00000000 # instruction | CALL putc | E8; next offset 80 + 178 = character output at 258.
11101011 11100000 # instruction | JMP read | EB; next offset 82 minus 32 = 50.
10000101 11001001 # instruction | TEST CX,CX | 85 C9 prevents backspace before the buffer starts.
01110100 11011100 # instruction | JZ read | 74; next offset 86 minus 36 = 50.
01001111 # instruction | DEC DI | 4F retreats the write pointer by one byte.
01001001 # instruction | DEC CX | 49 decrements input length.
10110000 00001000 # instruction | MOV AL,08 | B0 loads backspace for cursor movement.
11101000 10100101 00000000 # instruction | CALL putc | E8; next offset 93 + 165 = 258.
10110000 00100000 # instruction | MOV AL,20 | B0 loads a space to erase the character.
11101000 10100000 00000000 # instruction | CALL putc | E8; next offset 98 + 160 = 258.
