11101001 01001111 11111111 # instruction | JMP prompt | E9; next offset 216 minus 177 = 39.
10111110 10111100 01111111 # instruction | MOV SI,7FBC | BE loads unknown-command text at offset 444.
11101000 00011001 00000000 # instruction | CALL puts | E8; next offset 222 + 25 = 247.
11101001 01000110 11111111 # instruction | JMP prompt | E9; next offset 225 minus 186 = 39.
01010111 # instruction | PUSH DI | 57 preserves the caller's write pointer during string comparison.
10111111 00000000 10000010 # instruction | MOV DI,8200 | BF points to the command buffer.
10101100 # instruction | LODSB | AC fetches the next expected command byte.
00111010 00000101 # instruction | CMP AL,[DI] | 3A /r, ModR/M 05 selects AL and 16-bit memory at DS:DI.
01110101 00001001 # instruction | JNE unequal | 75; next offset 234 + 9 = 243.
01000111 # instruction | INC DI | 47 advances the command-buffer comparison pointer.
10000100 11000000 # instruction | TEST AL,AL | 84 C0 checks that matching included the terminating NUL.
01110101 11110110 # instruction | JNZ compare_next | 75; next offset 239 minus 10 = 229.
01011111 # instruction | POP DI | 5F restores the caller's pointer.
10110000 00000001 # instruction | MOV AL,01 | B0 returns true only for whole-string equality.
11000011 # instruction | RET | C3 returns to the command dispatcher.
01011111 # instruction | POP DI | 5F restores DI on the mismatch path too.
00110000 11000000 # instruction | XOR AL,AL | 30 C0 returns false on any mismatched byte.
11000011 # instruction | RET | C3 returns from unequal comparison.
10101100 # instruction | LODSB | AC fetches a string byte in puts.
10000100 11000000 # instruction | TEST AL,AL | 84 C0 checks the NUL terminator.
01110100 00000101 # instruction | JZ puts_done | 74; next offset 252 + 5 = RET at 257.
11101000 00000011 00000000 # instruction | CALL putc | E8; next offset 255 + 3 = 258.
11101011 11110110 # instruction | JMP puts | EB; next offset 257 minus 10 = 247.
11000011 # instruction | RET | C3 returns after the complete string.
01010000 # instruction | PUSH AX | 50 preserves caller AX in putc.
01010011 # instruction | PUSH BX | 53 preserves caller BX.
01010001 # instruction | PUSH CX | 51 preserves bounded keyboard length.
01010010 # instruction | PUSH DX | 52 preserves caller DX.
01010110 # instruction | PUSH SI | 56 preserves string pointer across BIOS calls.
01010111 # instruction | PUSH DI | 57 preserves keyboard write pointer.
01010000 # instruction | PUSH AX | 50 separately saves the character during BIOS video output.
10110100 00001110 # instruction | MOV AH,0E | B4 selects BIOS teletype.
10111011 00000111 00000000 # instruction | MOV BX,0007 | BB selects page zero and attribute seven.
11001101 00010000 # instruction | INT 10 | CD 10 prints the character on VGA.
01011000 # instruction | POP AX | 58 restores the character after BIOS output.
01010000 # instruction | PUSH AX | 50 saves the character during UART polling.
10111010 11111101 00000011 # instruction | MOV DX,03FD | BA selects UART line status.
11101100 # instruction | IN AL,DX | EC reads UART status.
10101000 00100000 # instruction | TEST AL,20 | A8 tests transmitter-ready bit.
01110100 11111011 # instruction | JZ serial_poll | 74 FB loops to IN, five bytes before the next instruction.
01011000 # instruction | POP AX | 58 restores the character.
10111010 11111000 00000011 # instruction | MOV DX,03F8 | BA selects serial transmit port.
11101110 # instruction | OUT DX,AL | EE writes the character to COM1.
01011111 # instruction | POP DI | 5F restores DI.
01011110 # instruction | POP SI | 5E restores SI.
01011010 # instruction | POP DX | 5A restores DX.
