01011011 # instruction | POP BX | 5B restores BX.
01011000 # instruction | POP AX | 58 restores AX.
11000011 # instruction | RET | C3 returns from putc with the caller registers restored.
01010000 # instruction | PUSH AX | 50 saves the full input byte for the low nibble.
01010001 # instruction | PUSH CX | 51 preserves caller's shift count.
10110001 00000100 # instruction | MOV CL,04 | B1 sets a four-bit shift count.
11010010 11101000 # instruction | SHR AL,CL | D2 /5; E8 selects AL; obtains the high nibble.
11101000 00000100 00000000 # instruction | CALL nibble | E8; next offset 303 + 4 = nibble encoder at 307.
01011001 # instruction | POP CX | 59 restores caller CX.
01011000 # instruction | POP AX | 58 restores the original byte.
00100100 00001111 # instruction | AND AL,0F | 24 imm8 masks the low nibble; fall through to its encoder.
00111100 00001010 # instruction | CMP AL,0A | 3C distinguishes digits 0–9 from hexadecimal A–F.
01110010 00000010 # instruction | JB decimal_digit | 72; next offset 311 + 2 = ASCII digit addition at 313.
00000100 00000111 # instruction | ADD AL,07 | 04 imm8 skips ASCII punctuation between 9 and A.
00000100 00110000 # instruction | ADD AL,30 | 04 imm8 adds ASCII zero, yielding uppercase hexadecimal.
